  "worked_solution": "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,-1) & =\\frac{3}{2(-1)^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2+1} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $P(3,-1)$ is the $1$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{x}{2{y}^{2}+1} & =1 \\\\ x & =2{y}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $P(3,-1)$ is the parabola $x=2{y}^{2}+1.$",
